n, and include or discuss the cyanohydrin-to-lactate competing branch.", "Attach direct Strecker and hydrolysis references to the corresponding reaction entries."]}, {"pathway_id": "P2", "reaction_scores": {"rxn_004": 0.87}, "chemical_feasibility": 0.87, "pathway_coherence": 0.88, "environmental_progression": 0.66, "target_achievement": 0.93, "overall_confidence": 0.82, "feedback": "Pulletikurti et al. (2022) support CO2-dependent conversion of alpha-ketoacids to amino acids using cyanide and ammonia. The deterministic check establishes that this reaction is balanceable; it is not classified as a conservation violation. Nevertheless, this lumped entry leaves the operative intermediates, final hydrolysis conditions and carbon/nitrogen accounting insufficiently specified. Listing ammonia and CO2 on both sides does not establish their mechanistic or net stoichiometric roles.", "approved": true, "problematic_reactions": ["rxn_004"], "suggestions": ["Provide explicit experimentally justified coefficients and distinguish required initial CO2 from any CO2 evolved during the transformation.", "Identify the hydantoin/N-carbamoyl sequence described in the supplied research, either through intermediate nodes or a documented lumped mechanism.", "Specify pH, temperature, reagent concentrations and the conditions that release free alanine rather than merely an alanine precursor."]}, {"pathway_id": "P3", "reaction_scores": {"rxn_005": 0.93, "rxn_015": 0.94, "rxn_016": 0.95}, "chemical_feasibility": 0.93, "pathway_coherence": 0.96, "environmental_progression": 0.66, "target_achievement": 0.97, "overall_confidence": 0.86, "feedback": "Native-iron reductive amination is experimentally motivated by Kitadai et al. (2019). Explicit Fe0 consumption and Fe2+ production correctly represent a finite reductant inventory, rather than an indefinitely operating catalyst. The lactate branch is appropriate, and ferrous hydroxide precipitation is correctly conditional. Missing ammonia activity, pH